// LoopOffloader is the optional capability of a LoopHandler that offloads
// blocking work (R3). At Start the server walks the chain by Next for the
// first offloader whose Worker is not nil, starts one worker goroutine per
// lane, and calls OnOutbound once, after LoopStarter.OnStart and before any
// other callback. Each job a lane sends comes back through OnDone, on that
// lane's thread, once Work has returned; a job whose connection closed
// meanwhile comes back too, so the offloader frees what it kept for it. A
// draining loop keeps open every connection Pending names. The workers stop
// after the loop engine has: on Shutdown once the drain is over, queued jobs
// then dropped.
